### SevaSetu — all 29 endpoints, in plan order. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension
### (or JetBrains HTTP Client). Every request goes to the gateway, which checks the token and sets
### x-user-id / x-user-role for the services.
###
### 1. Set @gw (deployed gateway, local A gateway :8080, or B's mock gateway :8090 from `npm run dev`).
### 2. Run "2. demo-login" once per user and paste each token below.

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@vol = paste-seeded-volunteer-token
@vol2 = paste-circle-member-token
@newvol = paste-new-volunteer-token
@coord = paste-coordinator-token

# fixed seed ids (shared/ids.js)
@seededVolunteer = 650000000000000000000002
@newVolunteer = 650000000000000000000001
@circleMember = 650000000000000000000003
@coordinator = 650000000000000000000004
@needId = 650000000000000000000021
@visitId = 650000000000000000000031
@commitmentId = 650000000000000000000041

### Health — every service (R1: reflect true, bridge true)
GET {{gw}}/health/all

########################################################################
### Person A — core-service (endpoints 1–20)
### Paths and rules are from A's plan. Bodies of 11 and 17 follow the plan's wording; check them
### against A's final routes.
########################################################################

### 1. All demo users (public)
GET {{gw}}/api/auth/users

### 2. Demo login (public) → { token, user }
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{seededVolunteer}}" }

### 3. Who am I
GET {{gw}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 4. Needs search (max 3, with fitReason)
GET {{gw}}/api/needs?day=Saturday&maxKm=5&interest=teaching
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 5. One need
GET {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 6. Publish a need (coordinator; consent.readBack must be true). Body = B's draft + consent (B3)
POST {{gw}}/api/needs
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "English Reading Support",
  "want": "A group of 12 students from class 6 to 8 would like help to read English aloud with confidence.",
  "serveUsWell": "Come on time every Saturday. Listen before you correct.",
  "youWillLearn": "How patience helps a young reader find their own voice.",
  "groupSize": 12,
  "interestTags": ["teaching", "reading"],
  "rhythm": { "day": "Saturday", "start": "10:30", "end": "12:00" },
  "weeks": 4,
  "place": "Government School, Kanchipuram",
  "consent": { "readBack": true, "agreedOn": "2026-10-06" }
}

### 7. Request a Listen-First visit (volunteer)
POST {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}/visits
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 8. My visits (volunteer: own; coordinator: for their needs)
GET {{gw}}/api/visits/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 9. What I heard
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/{{visitId}}/heard
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "heardText": "They want to read stories they choose themselves." }

### 10. Decision (volunteer or coordinator)
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/{{visitId}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "yes": true }

### 11. Commit (visit must be agreed)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "visitId": "{{visitId}}", "sentence": "I will come every Saturday for four weeks." }

### 12. My commitments
GET {{gw}}/api/commitments/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 13. One commitment (currentWeek, weeks, sessions) — B's diary reads the week from here
GET {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 14. I cannot come this week
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/absence
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "week": 3 }

### 15. Cover for a circle member
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/cover
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "week": 3 }

### 16. Coordinator sends the invitation
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/invitation
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Would you like to keep coming for four more weeks?" }

### 17. Continue / pause / finish
PATCH {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/continue
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "choice": "continue" }

### 18. My circle
GET {{gw}}/api/circles/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 19. Coordinator overview (needs, pending visits, week grid)
GET {{gw}}/api/coordinator/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 20. Demo time travel
POST {{gw}}/api/demo/advance
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "toWeek": 4 }

########################################################################
### Person B — reflect-service (endpoints 21–27)
########################################################################

### R2: no token → 401
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}

### 21. This week's question (R3 week 1 = patience; R4 try 2, 3, 4, 5)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/question?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}&week=1
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 21. R5: no week → 400
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/question?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 22. Save week 2 (R7 → 201). Send again with other text → 200, still one week-2 entry (R8)
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "questionId": "", "text": "I waited, and he finished the sentence himself.", "hardDay": false }

### 22. R9: empty text → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "text": "" }

### 22. R12: VOL2 sends VOL's userId in the body → saved under VOL2; VOL's list unchanged
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "text": "Written by someone else", "userId": "{{seededVolunteer}}" }

### 23. My entries, week order (R6: exactly 1 after seeding)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 23. R10: another volunteer → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}

### 23. R11: coordinator → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 24. Then and Now (R13)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/then-and-now?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 24. R14: a commitment with no entries → { first: null, latest: null }
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/then-and-now?commitmentId=650000000000000000000099
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 25. Wisdom for today (R15: same twice, has source)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/today
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 26. All wisdom (R16: 8 items)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 26. One theme (service, strength, patience, work)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom?theme=patience
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27. Why? (R17: no-ranks, no-photos, no-hours, listen-first)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/why/no-ranks
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27. R18: unknown rule → 404
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/why/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

########################################################################
### Person B — bridge-service (endpoints 28–29)
########################################################################

### 28. Draft from English (B1: 9 keys, source "ai" when GROQ_API_KEY is set, else "fallback")
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "12 students of class 6 to 8 want help reading English aloud, Saturday mornings at the government school in Kanchipuram", "language": "en" }

### 28. Draft from Tamil (B2: English draft, groupSize 12)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "காஞ்சிபுரம் அரசுப் பள்ளியில் 6 முதல் 8 ஆம் வகுப்பு படிக்கும் 12 மாணவர்கள் சனிக்கிழமை காலை ஆங்கிலம் உரக்கப் படிக்க உதவி வேண்டும்", "language": "ta" }

### 28. B4: volunteer → 403
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "12 students want help reading", "language": "en" }

### 28. B5: empty text → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "" }

### 28. B6 / B7: privacy flags (at least 2) and no person in the draft
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Ravi, a poor boy, father's income is Rs 5000", "language": "en" }

### 29. Speech to text (B12). Put a real base64 16 kHz mono WAV in "audio".
###     PowerShell: [Convert]::ToBase64String([IO.File]::ReadAllBytes("tamil-16khz.wav"))
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/transcribe
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "audio": "UklGRiQAAABXQVZFZm10IBAAAAABAAEAgD4AAAB9AAACABAAZGF0YQAAAAA=", "language": "ta", "samplingRate": 16000 }

### 29. B13: no audio → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/transcribe
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
